# ============================================================
#  Expansion — more character events (social slot).
#  Three each for Lyra, Tobias, Seraphine, Corvin, Mir, Nessa,
#  Kael; two for Bram.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Lyra ----------------

@event lyra_toast
title: Lyra Cannot Cook
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 9
weight: 10
art: flame
tags: social
scene: A dormitory kitchenette full of smoke, a crimson-haired girl holding a blackened slice of toast at arm's length, a fire-charm still sparking in her other hand.
text: Smoke pours from the kitchenette. Lyra Vaneshade, pyromancy prodigy, is holding a piece of bread that is now mostly charcoal. "I can incinerate a target at forty paces," she says. "I cannot make toast. Don't. Say. Anything."
> left: Say absolutely nothing
  rel lyra +small
  say: You open a window, take the bread, and make two perfect slices with a toasting fork. She eats hers in dignified silence. Then she asks for another.
> right: Teach her — gently
  mood -tiny
  rel lyra +medium
  spark lyra +tiny
  charm +tiny
  say: "Less fire," you say. "No, less. Less than that." It takes eleven slices. On the twelfth, she makes perfect golden toast and looks prouder than after any duel.

@event lyra_mother_visit
title: Lady Vaneshade
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: rel(lyra) >= 15 and year >= 2
weight: 12
art: crown
tags: social rival
scene: A tall woman in crimson and black walking through the courtyard like a queen inspecting troops, Lyra two steps behind her, very straight.
text: Lady Vaneshade has come to inspect the academy, and her daughter. She stops in front of you. "You must be the one my daughter mentions," she says. "Constantly. I'd like to know why."
> left: Answer with perfect manners
  challenge negotiate journeyman +1 if has(origin_noble):
    win:
      rel lyra +large
      renown +small
      say: You are polite, precise and unimpressed. Lady Vaneshade studies you, then says, "Hm. Adequate." Lyra looks at you like you've slain a dragon.
    lose:
      rel lyra +small
      mood -small
      say: You stumble over a title. Lady Vaneshade's eyebrow says everything. Later, Lyra finds you. "She does that to everyone," she says. "You lasted longer than most."
> right: Answer honestly
  mood -tiny
  rel lyra +medium
  if spark(lyra) >= 15:
    spark lyra +small
  say: "Because she's brilliant," you say, "and nobody tells her." Lady Vaneshade is silent. Lyra is redder than her hair. The visit ends early.

@event lyra_rival_respect
title: Respect, Grudgingly
class: milestone
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: lyra
when: bond(lyra) == "rival" and rel(lyra) >= 9
weight: 16
art: flame
tags: rival social
scene: Two rivals sitting on the edge of a scorched practice ring, wands laid down between them, sharing a flask of water.
text: After another draw, Lyra drops onto the edge of the ring beside you. "You're the only person here who makes me better," she says, as if confessing a crime. "I hate it. I don't want it to stop."
> left: "Then let's keep it a rivalry."
  rel lyra +medium
  say: "Good," she says, relieved. "Rivalry I understand." She shoves you, lightly. You shove her back. The rivalry continues, warmer.
> right: "Or we could just be friends."
  bond lyra friend
  rel lyra +large
  say: She considers the word like an unfamiliar spell. "Friends," she says. "Fine. But I'm still going to beat you." You'd be disappointed if she didn't.

# ---------------- Tobias ----------------

@event tobias_scarecrow
title: The Scarecrow Project
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 6
weight: 10
art: leaf
tags: social nature
scene: A scarecrow in a straw hat waving its arms at crows in a vegetable patch, a big farm boy and a student watching it proudly.
text: Tobias has built a scarecrow for the greenhouse plots and wants to enchant it to scare crows. "Just a little life," he says. "Just enough to wave. Nothing creepy."
> left: Help enchant it
  challenge spell apprentice:
    win:
      rel tobias +medium
      say: The scarecrow waves. It also learns to wave hello, and to tip its hat to the headmistress. The crows are terrified. The first-years adore it.
    lose:
      rel tobias +small
      mood -tiny
      say: The scarecrow comes to life, looks at you both, and walks off into the forest. You see it sometimes, at dusk, waving.
> right: Suggest a cat instead
  rel tobias +small
  say: You borrow the greenhouse cat. The crows leave immediately. Tobias is a little sad about the scarecrow, so you help him make it a hat.

@event tobias_dance_lessons
title: Two Left Feet
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 9 and (month == 3 or month == 4)
weight: 12
art: music
tags: social romance
scene: An empty classroom with desks pushed to the walls, a big boy counting steps aloud, a broom propped against the wall as his former partner.
text: Tobias has pushed the desks against the walls of an empty classroom. "The Ball's {month == 4: tonight|next month}," he says, mortified. "I've been practising with a broom. The broom has complained."
> left: Teach him to waltz
  health -tiny
  rel tobias +medium
  spark tobias +tiny
  charm +tiny
  say: One-two-three, one-two-three. He steps on you exactly fifty times. On the fifty-first bar, something clicks, and for a moment he's graceful. He looks astonished.
> right: Tell him nobody cares about footwork
  rel tobias +tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: "Just enjoy it," you say. He thinks about this, nods, and dances like a delighted bear. It's terrible. It's wonderful.

@event tobias_storm_greenhouse
time: night
title: Storm Over the Greenhouses
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: tobias
when: rel(tobias) >= 12 and month >= 6 and month <= 8
weight: 12
art: bolt
tags: nature danger
scene: Rain lashing a glass greenhouse at night, panes cracking, a big boy holding a door shut against the wind while plants rattle inside.
text: A storm hits at midnight. Glass is cracking in the greenhouses. Tobias is out there in his nightshirt, trying to hold a door shut against the wind with his whole body. "The moonflowers!" he shouts. "Eleven years!"
> left: Run out and help
  health -small
  alignment +tiny
  rel tobias +large
  spark tobias +tiny
  say: You hold the panes together with every shielding charm you know until dawn. Every moonflower survives. Tobias hugs you, soaked, laughing, half crying.
> right: Fetch Old Maud
  health -tiny
  rel tobias +small
  rel maud +small
  say: Maud arrives in her dressing gown, mutters three words at the sky, and the wind politely goes elsewhere. Tobias stares at her. "Teach me that," he says.
> up[heartwood]: Grow a tree to shelter the glass
  health -tiny
  rel tobias +large
  spark tobias +tiny
  say: You kneel in the mud and a tree comes up between the wind and the greenhouse, and spreads its branches over the glass. The storm breaks on it all night. In the morning Tobias sits under it with you and doesn't say anything at all.

# ---------------- Seraphine ----------------

@event seraphine_lost_day
title: Seraphine Is Tomorrow
class: routine
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: rel(seraphine) >= 6
weight: 10
art: hourglass
tags: mystery social
scene: A girl sitting at the wrong desk in an empty classroom, a teacup in her hands, the calendar on the wall showing the next day's date.
text: Seraphine is sitting in an empty classroom, waiting for a lesson that's happening tomorrow. "I've slipped," she says calmly. "I'm a day ahead. It happens. I need someone to remind me what today is."
> left: Talk her back into today
  rel seraphine +medium
  lore +tiny
  say: You tell her what you had for breakfast, what the weather's like, what Thorne said this morning. Slowly her eyes stop looking through you. "Oh," she says. "Hello. Today."
> right: Ask her what tomorrow holds
  chance even:
    study +tiny
    say: "There's a surprise quiz in every class," she says. "They planned it together. Question three is always a trick." It is, every time. You get them all right.
  else:
    mood -tiny
    say: "It rains," she says. "You get wet. You'll be fine." You are not fine. You get very wet.

@event seraphine_painting
title: A Painting of Somewhere Else
class: routine
tone: eerie
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: rel(seraphine) >= 12
weight: 10
art: eye
tags: social mystery
scene: A small canvas on an easel showing a stranger's cottage by the sea, a girl with paint on her fingers watching someone look at it.
text: Seraphine has painted a small cottage by the sea, with a crooked chimney and a blue door. "It's yours," she says. "In twelve years. I thought you should see it now. In case you want a different door."
> left: Keep the painting
  chance likely:
    mood +small
    rel seraphine +medium
    say: You hang it over your bed. Some nights you swear the smoke from the chimney moves. You decide, privately, that you like the blue door.
  else:
    rel seraphine +small
    mood -tiny
    say: You hang it over your bed. Some mornings the door is a different colour, and you lie there wondering which one you chose.
> right: Ask her to paint her own future
  rel seraphine +medium
  spark seraphine +tiny
  say: She looks at the blank canvas for a long time. "I never can," she says. "Seers can't see themselves." Then, quietly: "Unless someone's standing next to us."

@event seraphine_mother
title: The Oracle's Summons
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: seraphine
when: rel(seraphine) >= 15 and year >= 2
weight: 12
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A girl holding a letter that glows faintly silver, standing at the top of a tower stair, looking down as if about to fall or fly.
text: Seraphine's mother, the Oracle of Vell, wants her home to take up the family seat. "I'd spend my life telling kings what they want to hear," Seraphine says. "But she's already seen me say yes. She always sees me say yes."
> left: "Then surprise her."
  mood -tiny
  rel seraphine +large
  say: Seraphine writes back: no. For a whole day she's terrified, and so are you. Then she's giddy. "I didn't see that coming," she keeps saying. "I didn't see it coming!"
> right: "Maybe she's right."
  rel seraphine -medium
  say: She nods slowly. She doesn't go — not yet. But for a long while she stops telling you her visions, and you miss them more than you expected.

# ---------------- Corvin ----------------

@event corvin_confiscation_vault
title: The Confiscation Vault
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) >= 12
weight: 12
art: lock
tags: social danger
scene: A dark vault crammed with confiscated student contraband — fanged frisbees, cursed dice, a goblet of endless soup — two figures with a lantern at the door.
text: "The confiscation vault," Corvin breathes. "Three hundred years of everything the faculty ever took off a student. My grandfather's lucky deck is in there. I just want it back. Lookout?"
> left: Keep lookout
  alignment -tiny
  challenge deceive adept-:
    win:
      rel corvin +large
      gold +small
      say: He comes out with the deck and a handful of confiscated coins "for your trouble". The deck is, it turns out, genuinely lucky. He wins at cards for a month.
    lose:
      gain detention
      rel corvin +medium
      say: The vault alarm is a very loud goblin. You both spend a week cataloguing contraband — which Corvin considers a victory.
> right: Talk him out of it
  rel corvin -tiny
  challenge negotiate vs corvin.guile:
    win:
      rel corvin +medium
      say: You convince him to just ask Thorne. Thorne, astonishingly, gives it back. "Your grandfather cheated me with it in '41," he says. "Tell him I said hello."
    lose:
      say: He goes anyway, alone. He comes back with the deck and a black eye from the goblin. Worth it, he says.

@event corvin_brother
title: Corvin's Brother
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) >= 15 and year >= 2
weight: 12
art: mask
tags: social money
scene: A rough-looking young man leaning on the academy gate, cap pulled low, Corvin facing him with his hands in his pockets.
text: There's a rough-looking man at the gates, and Corvin has gone very still. "My brother," he says. "He wants money. He always wants money. If I don't pay, he tells the headmistress where I learned to pick locks."
> left: Help Corvin face him down
  alignment +small
  challenge negotiate journeyman:
    win:
      rel corvin +large
      say: You stand beside Corvin while he says no — the first time, he tells you later, that he's ever said it. His brother leaves. Corvin sits down on the steps and laughs and shakes.
    lose:
      rel corvin +medium
      mood -small
      say: It turns ugly. In the end you empty your purse into his hand, just to make him leave. Corvin presses every coin back into yours that evening, with a strange new seriousness.
> right: Stay out of family business
  rel corvin -small
  say: Corvin pays. You see him counting out every coin he has. He's quiet for a long while after.

@event corvin_cards
title: How to Cheat at Cards
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: corvin
when: rel(corvin) >= 6
weight: 10
art: cards
tags: social money
scene: A candlelit table in a corner of the common room, a boy fanning a deck of cards with a flourish, a student watching his hands very closely.
text: "Rule one: never cheat," says Corvin, shuffling so fast the cards blur. "Rule two: if you're going to cheat, never get caught. Rule three: I'm about to teach you how they cheat, so you never lose to them."
> left: Learn the tricks
  guile +small
  rel corvin +small
  say: By midnight you can spot a marked card, a bottom deal and a mirror charm. You will never be fleeced at Wizard's Hand again.
> right: Learn to play honestly — and well
  when: gold >= 3
  chance likely:
    lore +tiny
    rel corvin +small
    gold +small
    say: He teaches you odds and nerve instead. That weekend you win eight crowns at the common-room game without cheating. Corvin is weirdly proud.
  else:
    gold -tiny
    lore +tiny
    rel corvin +small
    say: He teaches you odds and nerve instead. That weekend the odds take three crowns off you. "Also a lesson," says Corvin.
  if knows(corvin.sundays):
    rel corvin +tiny
    say: Near the end he shuffles the slow way, the rainy-Sunday way, and you say you know whose shuffle it is. He doesn't answer. He deals you in anyway, for good.

# ---------------- Mir ----------------

@event mir_ornithopter
title: The Test Flight
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: mir
when: rel(mir) >= 9
weight: 12
art: gear
tags: social danger
scene: A rickety winged contraption balanced on the edge of a tower roof, a goggled artificer strapping into it, a friend holding a rope.
text: Mir has built a flying machine with canvas wings and seven propellers. It is balanced on the edge of the north tower. "Brooms are so last century," they say, strapping in. "I need someone on the rope. Probably. Possibly."
> left: Hold the rope
  challenge feat apprentice wild:
    win:
      rel mir +large
      renown +small
      say: The machine flies — wobbly, loud, glorious — twice around the tower before landing in the lake. Mir surfaces whooping. You're both legends by dinner.
    lose:
      health -medium
      rel mir +medium
      say: The rope wins. You are dragged eight feet along the roof before letting go. The machine lands in a tree. Mir waves from it, delighted.
> right: Insist on a safety net
  rel mir +small
  alchemy +tiny
  say: You spend a day building a net. The machine flies four feet and drops into it. "Data!" says Mir happily. Nobody dies. It's a good day.

@event mir_lab_fire
title: Fire in the Workshop
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: mir
when: rel(mir) >= 12
weight: 10
art: flame
tags: danger
scene: A workshop full of smoke and orange light, notebooks scattered across a burning bench, a figure in goggles coughing in the doorway.
text: The workshop is on fire. Properly this time. Mir is in the doorway, coughing — and trying to go back in. "My notebooks! Three years of notes!"
> left: Grab the notebooks
  alignment +tiny
  challenge feat apprentice+ wild:
    win:
      rel mir +large
      health -small
      say: You come out singed, smoking, with an armful of notebooks. Mir stares at you, then at the notebooks, then bursts into tears and hugs you, both of you coughing.
    lose:
      health -large
      rel mir +medium
      say: You get halfway before the smoke drives you back. You save one notebook. Mir says it's the most important one. You both know it isn't. They mean it anyway.
> right: Drag Mir away
  alignment +tiny
  rel mir +medium
  health -tiny
  say: You haul Mir back from the door. The notebooks burn. Mir is silent for a week. Then they start a new notebook. The first page just says: "Thank you."
  if knows(mir.corridor):
    rel mir +tiny
    say: The next morning you find them soldering on the corridor floor outside the burnt door, and bring them a cushion, and tea.
> up[hoarfrost]: Freeze the fire out
  alignment +tiny
  rel mir +large
  health -tiny
  say: You throw frost at the doorway until the flames grey over and give up with a hiss. The notebooks are wet, cold and whole. Mir hugs them, then you, then the notebooks again, shivering.

@event mir_name_day
title: Mir's Name Day
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: mir
when: rel(mir) >= 15
weight: 10
art: gem
tags: social
scene: A cluttered workshop decorated with paper chains and one small cake with a single gear-shaped candle, an artificer looking embarrassed and pleased.
text: It's Mir's name day. They mention it casually, as if it doesn't matter. It clearly matters. Nobody else seems to know.
> left: Throw a surprise party
  gold -small
  rel mir +large
  mood +small
  say: Six friends, one cake and a banner you painted badly. Mir walks in, stops, and has to sit down. "Nobody's ever..." they start, and can't finish.
> right: Give them a handmade gift
  rel mir +medium
  spark mir +tiny
  say: A little brass key that fits nothing. "For whatever you build next," you say. Mir wears it on a chain, every day, for years.

# ---------------- Nessa ----------------

@event nessa_headmistress_interview
title: The Impossible Interview
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: rel(nessa) >= 9 and (met(isolde) and rel(isolde) >= 6)
weight: 12
art: paper
tags: social
scene: A newspaper editor and a student waiting outside the headmistress's tower door, the editor clutching a list of questions three pages long.
text: "Nobody has interviewed the headmistress in twenty years," Nessa says. "But she likes you. Probably. Get me in the door and I'll name my firstborn after you."
> left: Ask the headmistress
  rel isolde -tiny
  challenge negotiate journeyman +1 if renown >= 25:
    win:
      rel nessa +large
      renown +medium
      say: The headmistress agrees to ten minutes. She gives Nessa forty, and gives you a look that says you have spent a favour. The interview runs on the front page and sells out three printings.
    lose:
      rel nessa +small
      say: "No," says the headmistress, pleasantly. "But tell Miss Quill her piece on the kitchens was excellent." Nessa frames the rejection. The headmistress is a shade cooler with you in the corridors after that.
> right: Suggest someone overlooked instead
  rel nessa +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: Nessa interviews the night porter instead. It's the most-read piece of the year. Half the academy cries over breakfast.

@event nessa_typo
time: morning
title: A Catastrophic Typo
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: rel(nessa) >= 6 and met(thorne)
weight: 10
art: paper
tags: social
scene: A newspaper with a single word circled in red ink, an editor with her head in her hands, a stack of papers still warm from the press.
text: The Ledger has gone to print. In the profile of Professor Thorne, a single wrong letter has turned "Thorne: Still Lively" into "Thorne: Still Lovely". By breakfast the whole academy will be calling the most frightening man in the castle lovely. Five hundred copies.
> left: Help her fix every copy overnight
  health -tiny
  rel nessa +medium
  say: You correct five hundred copies with a scraping charm and a lot of tea. At dawn, Nessa falls asleep on the press. Thorne never knows.
  if knows(nessa.planted):
    rel nessa +tiny
    say: At dawn you ask whether this was one of her planted errors. "No," she says, horrified, and then laughs until she cries.
> right: Tell her to run a correction and own it
  mood -tiny
  rel nessa +small
  rel thorne +small
  say: The correction is gracious. Thorne, astonishingly, cuts it out and pins it to his door. "Precision," he says in class, "is a virtue. So is apology."

@event nessa_burnout
time: evening night
title: The Editor Sleeps
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: nessa
when: rel(nessa) >= 12 and year >= 2
weight: 10
art: candle
tags: social
scene: A girl asleep at a desk in a newspaper office, her self-writing quill still scratching on its own, the candle burned down to a stub.
text: Nessa hasn't slept properly in a week. She's asleep at her desk now, and her quill — unsupervised — is still writing next week's paper. It has started inventing news.
> left: Put her to bed and run the paper yourself
  health -tiny
  rel nessa +large
  study -small
  say: You edit, typeset and print one issue, and miss a day of classes doing it. It's adequate. When Nessa wakes she reads it, winces at your headlines, and hugs you for a long time.
> right: Wake her and make her rest
  mood -tiny
  rel nessa +medium
  say: She argues for ten minutes, then sleeps for fourteen hours. The quill's invented news about a dragon in the kitchens turns out to be true.

# ---------------- Kael ----------------

@event kael_northern_lights
time: night
title: The Lights of the North
class: routine
tone: warm
trigger: social
actor: kael
when: rel(kael) >= 12 and (month <= 5 or month >= 12)
weight: 12
art: star
tags: social romance
scene: Two figures on a frozen hillside under ribbons of green and violet light, one pointing upward, frost forming a circle around them.
text: Kael wakes you at midnight. "Come," he says. On the hill above the lake, the sky is moving — green and violet ribbons, the lights of his home, here, for him. "I called them," he says. "I wanted you to see."
> left: Watch in silence
  health -tiny
  rel kael +small
  mood +medium
  say: You watch until the lights fade. Neither of you speaks. On the walk down, he takes your hand without seeming to notice he's done it.
> right: Ask him about home
  health -tiny
  rel kael +medium
  lore +small
  say: He tells you about ice palaces and singing glaciers and a mother who never once said she was proud. Then he says: "This place is more home now." He means the hill. He means you.
  spark kael +tiny

@event kael_fever
title: Kael Burns
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: kael
when: rel(kael) >= 9
weight: 10
art: rain
tags: danger social
scene: A pale boy in a narrow bed, sweating, frost forming and melting on the pillow around his head in a constant cycle.
text: Kael has a fever — and for someone made of frost, a fever is dangerous. The infirmary's warming charms are making it worse. Sister Amaranth looks frightened. "He needs cold," she says. "Real cold. I don't know where to get it."
> left: Bring him snow from the mountain
  alignment +tiny
  challenge feat journeyman+:
    win:
      rel kael +large
      health -medium
      say: You fly to the peaks on a borrowed broom and come back with a sack of ancient snow. By morning his fever breaks. He doesn't let go of your sleeve all day.
    lose:
      health -large
      rel kael +medium
      say: The mountain wins. You come back half-frozen and empty-handed. Kael recovers anyway, slowly — and visits you in the next bed.
  if knows(kael.cold_hands):
    rel kael +tiny
    say: Later you remember that his hands were warm when you left, for the first time since you've known him, and how much that frightened you.
> right: Send word to Ilse
  if met(ilse) and not flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north):
    rel kael +medium
    rel ilse +medium
    say: Ilse arrives in a whirl of snow, puts her hand on his forehead and says something sharp in Northern. The fever breaks. Kael stares at his sister for a long time.
  else:
    rel kael +small
    say: You can't find her. Kael recovers slowly, on his own, the way he's always done everything.

@event kael_letter_home
title: A Letter He Won't Send
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: kael
when: rel(kael) >= 15 and flag(kael_told)
weight: 10
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A boy at a library desk, a letter half-written in sharp Northern script, a candle beside it, ink frozen in the pen.
text: Kael is writing a letter. He's rewritten the first line eleven times. "To my mother," he says. "I'm telling her I won't come home. I won't open the door. I'm telling her I've found..." He stops.
> left: "Found what?"
  rel kael +medium
  spark kael +tiny
  say: He looks at you for a long time. Then he writes the last word of the sentence without showing you, seals it, and sends it. He's lighter for days.
> right: Help him find the words
  health -tiny
  rel kael +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You sit together until the candle's gone. The letter, when it's finished, is short. It doesn't apologise once. He sends it at dawn.

# ---------------- Bram ----------------

@event bram_father_visit
title: Bram's Father
class: routine
tone: light
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: flag(bram_softened) and rel(bram) >= 9
weight: 14
art: shield
tags: social
scene: A towering grey-haired man in an old head-boy's sash speaking down to a red-faced prefect in the entrance hall, students hurrying past pretending not to look.
text: A tall man in an old head-boy's sash is speaking to Bram in the entrance hall, quietly and terribly. Bram has shrunk two sizes. "...never amount to anything," the man is saying.
> left: Interrupt — say something good
  challenge negotiate apprentice+:
    win:
      rel bram +large
      say: You tell his father {seen(bram_turns): about the night at the boathouse|what Bram is like when nobody's keeping score}. The man falls silent. Bram looks at you like you've handed him a sword.
    lose:
      rel bram +medium
      say: His father looks through you as if you're furniture. But afterwards, Bram finds you and says, roughly, "Nobody's ever stood there before. Thanks."
> right: Find Bram afterwards
  mood -tiny
  rel bram +medium
  say: He's behind the stables, again. You sit on the bucket next to his. You don't talk. After a while he says, "Same time next year, probably," and almost laughs.
  if knows(bram.portrait):
    rel bram +tiny
    say: On the way back you take him the long way round, so you don't pass the corridor of head boys. He notices, and says nothing, which from Bram is thanks.

@event bram_cheating
title: Bram Cheats
class: routine
tone: tense
trigger: social
actor: bram
when: met(bram) and (month == 4 or month == 10)
weight: 10
art: scroll
tags: rival study
scene: A prefect in an exam hall slipping a tiny scroll out of his sleeve, a student two desks away watching.
text: In the exam hall, two desks away, you see Bram Hollis — prefect, enforcer of rules — slip a tiny scroll out of his sleeve. He sees you seeing him. His face goes white.
> left: Report him
  rel bram -huge
  rel isolde +small
  renown +small
  alignment +small
  say: Bram loses his sash for the rest of the year. Some students cheer. You don't feel like cheering. Neither, later, does he.
> right: Say nothing — and let him know you saw
  alignment -tiny
  rel bram +medium
  guile +small
  say: After the exam you just look at him. He nods, once. You never mention it. But his demerits stop, for you and for everyone you know.
